              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does blast film require an attachment system?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>For blast mitigation applications, attachment systems that anchor the filmed glass to the frame are strongly recommended — they keep the filmed pane in the opening during a blast event rather than allowing it to push out. We assess your frame type and include attachment recommendations in every blast mitigation proposal.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can blast film be installed on existing glass?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes. Blast mitigation film is a retrofit solution applied to existing glass. We assess glass type, age, frame condition, and compatibility before specifying a system. For historic government buildings with single-pane glass where replacement is not feasible, blast film provides a non-destructive security upgrade.</div>
              </div>
