            <div class="of-ftype__step">03</div>
            <h2 class="of-ftype__title">Ballistic-Resistant System.
Retrofit. Not Bulletproof.</h2>
            <p class="of-ftype__desc">The C-Bond BRS (Ballistic Resistant System) pairs multi-layer PET security film with C-Bond Secure nanotechnology primer. The primer fills microscopic glass defects and improves adhesion — the combined system delays and resists projectile penetration. UL 752 tested system context. A retrofit alternative to ballistic glass for military installations, armories, and critical infrastructure.</p>
            <div class="of-ftype__faq">
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Is ballistic-resistant film bulletproof?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>No. Ballistic-resistant film delays and resists projectile penetration — it is not bulletproof glass. Only a tested system can be described by a specific resistance rating such as UL 752. Standard security film should never be described as stopping bullets. We verify current C-Bond documentation and test data before specifying any ballistic system.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What is C-Bond Secure primer?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>C-Bond Secure is a nanotechnology mounting primer applied to glass before film installation. It fills microscopic glass defects and improves adhesion, clarity, and cure behavior. It is not a stand-alone ballistic film — it supports the multi-layer PET security film system as part of the C-Bond BRS.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">When is a ballistic system appropriate?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Ballistic-resistant film systems are specified for facilities facing documented projectile threat levels — military installations, armories, law enforcement facilities, and critical infrastructure. A threat assessment is required before selecting a ballistic system. We work with your security team to match the system to your threat profile and provide test documentation.</div>
