Daytime Concealment.</h2>
            <p class="of-ftype__desc">One-way reflective security film provides daytime privacy for sensitive operations — evidence rooms, secure offices, and confidential processing areas. The exterior appears reflective during daylight hours while those inside maintain full outward views. Combines visual privacy with fragment retention and forced entry delay.</p>
            <div class="of-ftype__faq">
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does one-way privacy work at night?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>One-way mirror film relies on a brightness differential — it reverses at night when interior lights are on. For 24/7 privacy in areas used after dark, frosted security film is available. We assess your operational hours and recommend the right privacy solution for each area of your facility.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can privacy film still provide security?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes. Privacy security films are built on the same thick PET base as clear security film — the reflective or tinted layer is integrated without reducing impact resistance. You get fragment retention, delayed entry, and visual privacy in one installation.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does it affect the building's appearance?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Reflective security film gives the building a consistent, professional mirrored appearance from the exterior. Clear security film is virtually invisible. We bring samples to every site visit so you can see exactly how each option looks on your glass before committing.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="of-ftype__cta">Explore privacy security options →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SLIDE 06: Anti-Graffiti -->
        <div class="of-ftype__slide" data-slide="5">
          <img src="/images/sb-slider-antigraffiti.jpg" alt="Anti-graffiti security window film protecting ground-floor glass of Philadelphia secured facility" title="Anti-graffiti security window film protecting ground-floor glass of secured facility" class="of-ftype__bg" />
          <div class="of-ftype__overlay"></div>
          <div class="of-ftype__content">
            <div class="of-ftype__step">06</div>
            <h2 class="of-ftype__title">Anti-Graffiti Film.
Protect. Peel. Replace.</h2>
            <p class="of-ftype__desc">Anti-graffiti film is a clear sacrificial layer applied to accessible exterior glass, lobby glazing, and ground-floor windows. When vandalized — scratched, acid-etched, or spray-painted — only the film is replaced, not the glass. Essential for Philadelphia secured facilities in high foot-traffic areas and transit-adjacent locations.</p>
            <div class="of-ftype__faq">
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How is anti-graffiti film different from security film?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Anti-graffiti film is optically clear with no tint or security properties — its sole purpose is to protect the glass surface from vandalism. It is applied as a sacrificial layer designed to be peeled off and replaced. Security film, by contrast, is thicker and designed for impact resistance and fragment retention. The two can be layered for comprehensive protection.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can it be applied to metal and mirrors?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes. Anti-graffiti film works on polished stainless steel, mirrors, and architectural metal surfaces in addition to glass. Elevator interiors, restroom mirrors, and lobby feature walls are common applications in Philadelphia secured facilities.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can it be combined with security film?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes. Anti-graffiti film can be applied as an outer sacrificial layer over security film for comprehensive protection — the anti-graffiti layer handles vandalism while the security layer provides impact resistance and fragment retention. We recommend this combination for ground-floor glass in high-traffic areas.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="of-ftype__cta">Get an anti-graffiti estimate →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

